  "what_this_kills": [
    "The rung. PLAN.md: 'If G-BOUNDARY fails, the rung dies here, with only the export spent.'",
    "The enabling fact. PLAN.md's settled-going-in row read: SAM 'does not merge tissue regions with foreign objects even where it over-segments tissue'. B2 = 0.3529 with CI upper bound 0.5294 is the direct refutation -- the whole interval sits below the 0.70 threshold."
  ],
  "what_the_gate_never_measured": {
    "finding": "PRECISION. B1 asks whether a mask exists over a foreign object (recall) and B2 whether that mask is sharp. Neither asks how many OTHER masks are present.",
    "raised_by": "legokna, 2026-08-12, on reading the adjudicated frames",
    "quantity": "SAM emits 13-50 instances per frame (RESULTS_ab_overlay.json) and masks the whole scene -- tissue, anatomy, instruments -- not only the foreign objects.",
    "consequence": "A VLM handed these masks receives references without identity: it can see that regions were marked, not which one is the foreign object. Consistent with the overlay's measured failure mode, which was identity substitution ('External drain' -> 'Needle', 'Needle' -> 'Clip'), not blindness.",
    "status": "A limitation of the PRE-REGISTRATION, not of the adjudication. A future gate on masks-as-input must carry a precision clause; B1/B2 alone cannot license the route even at 1.00."
  },
  "what_this_does_NOT_show": [
    "That SAM cannot FIND the objects. It does: B1 = 0.9714 on adjudicable frames, across all eight classes.",
    "That the metallic-clip objection decided anything. Clips scored covered 4/4. The concern that consumed 2026-08-11 -- in both its original (r = -0.17, RETIRED) and corrected forms -- turned out not to be the failure mode.",
    "That masks are useless as input generally. One mask source, one rendering; see context/decisions/input-side-access-was-never-the-bottleneck.md."
  ],
